Dear EPA, 
 
Please act swiftly and decisively and ban the use of lead in aviation fuel. 
 
This action is way overdue as lead has been banned from autos, paint and toys for decades. 
 
The FAA has stalled and only through action on the part of the EPA, local state and federal government, 
and the public will aviation do what they should have done many years ago. 
 
Airports are often close to schools, pre-schools, homes and playgrounds. We know that lead is unsafe at 
any level and particularly harmful to the developing brains of children. 
 
Aviation has continued to develop and produce new planes designed to use leaded fuel. There is no 
excuse for this, especially considering there are safe unleaded fuels available. 
 
The FAA must ramp up their testing and the industry must commit to making the switch. 
 
The children need more than lip service. They need regulations to protect them. 
 
Please act now. 
 
Thank you. 
 
