The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) is evaluating the impact of lead 
emissions from aircraft using leaded aviation gasoline in order to make a 
determination regarding whether aircraft lead emissions cause or contribute to air 
pollution which may reasonably be anticipated to endanger public health or 
welfare. 
 
The EPA currently intends to issue a proposed finding on the question of 
endangerment in 2017. This proposed finding will then undergo public notice and 
comment. After evaluating comments on the proposal, EPA plans to issue a final 
determination in 2018 (html) (still delayed as of September 2020). 
 
