I, HARRY FREITAS, declare as follows: 
1. 
I have personal knowledge of the facts set forth in this declaration.  If called as a 
witness, I could and would testify competently to the matters set forth herein. 
2. 
I graduated from San José State University in 1990, where I received a degree in Civil 
Engineering.  I am a Registered Professional Engineer licensed to practice in the State of California. 
3. 
Since 2017 I have been the Director of the County of Santa Clara (“County”) Roads and 
Airports Department, which, under the direction of the Santa Clara County Board of Supervisors 
(“Board”), is responsible for operation and maintenance of the County’s transportation 
infrastructure, including expressways, unincorporated roads and two general aviation airports: Reid-
Hillview Airport (“RHV”) and San Martin Airport (“E16”) (collectively “County Airports”).  The 
Airports Division of the Roads and Airports Department manages the County Airports, which 
includes renting the facilities at the airports to private individuals and businesses, setting the rules 
and regulations for operating aircraft and businesses at the County Airports, and providing services 
to aircraft operators, including the sale of fuel. 
4. 
Before becoming the Director of Roads and Airports, I was employed for 27 years with 
the City of San José, where I served as the Director of Planning, Building, and Code Enforcement, 
Assistant Director of Public Works, Deputy Director of Public Works, Division Manager, Associate 
Engineer, and Project Engineer in the Public Works Department, and a Senior Engineer in the 
Department of Transportation. 
5. 
I have reviewed the complaint filed on October 14, 2022, pursuant to 14 C.F.R. § 16 
titled Aircraft Owners and Pilots Association et al. v. County of Santa Clara, California 
(“Complaint”) which names as complainants Aircraft Owners and Pilots Association (“AOPA”), 
Aperture Aviation, Inc., Glynn Falcon, Robert A. Gingell, Christopher Luvara, Michael Luvara, Paul 
Marshall, Dr. Joseph C. McMurray, and Trade Winds Aviation (collectively “Complainants”). 
Reid Hillview Airport 
6. 
Reid Hillview Airport is a general aviation, public use airport located at 2500 
Cunningham Avenue in the City of San Jose, roughly three miles from downtown San Jose.  The 
County has owned and operated Reid Hillview Airport since 1961.  Since then, the County has 
