20. 
Unavailability of 100LL for purchase is a common condition at public use airports.  I 
have prepared a chart, attached hereto as Exhibit F, based on data downloaded on November 14, 
2022 from FAA’s Airport Data and Information Portal showing each of the 1,434 airports that 
reported general aviation “aircraft operations,” as defined in 14 CFR § 170.3, in the previous year 
where 100 octane avgas is not available for purchase.  Some select findings from the chart are as 
follows: 
a. There is no 100 octane avgas available for purchase at 70 out of a total 244 public 
use airports in California that reported general aviation aircraft operations. 
b. There were over four million aircraft operations in the past year from public use 
airports where 100 octane avgas is not available for purchase.   
c. Of the public use airports that reported general aviation aircraft operations in the 
previous year 45 exclusively sell a type of fuel other than 100 octane avgas.  Of 
these airports, 18 exclusively sell unleaded low octane avgas or automotive 
gasoline.   
Market Demand for Unleaded Avgas  
21. 
In addition to eliminating harmful lead emissions, the County expects that using the 
RHV Tanks and the E16 Tank (collectively, “County Tanks”) to sell unleaded avgas exclusively will  
allow it to meet significant market demand for unleaded avgas, and create a market that ensures a 
more reliable and affordable supply of UL94 in Northern California.   
22. 
I believe that there is a large underserved market for unleaded aviation fuel from 
aircraft operators in and around Santa Clara County.  There is limited availability of unleaded avgas 
in California.  By being one of the few providers of UL94, the County will be able to maximize its 
revenues from flowage fees and direct sales.  In contrast, 100LL is available for purchase at many 
local area airports, including Palo Alto Airport, Livermore Airport, San José International Airport, 
and Hollister Airport. 
23. 
Unleaded avgas provides many benefits to aircraft operators.  Unleaded avgas reduces 
lead deposits on the spark plugs valves and pistons and lengthens the intervals between oil changes 
and engine maintenance.   
