25. 
Dedicating four tanks at RHV and one tank at E16 to the exclusive sale of UL94 
allowed the County Airports to offer UL94 at a reduced price to aircraft operators.  UL94 is 
manufactured in Indiana.  Purchasing UL94 in smaller quantities would require transport by truck.  
Purchasing UL94 in larger quantities allows for transport by rail at a reduced cost.  Dedicating four 
tanks at RHV and one tank at E16 to the exclusive sale of UL94 and purchasing in conjunction with 
other airports has made rail transport of UL94 feasible.  The net savings due to bulk purchase is 
approximately $1.15 per gallon, a significant savings.   
26. 
Being able to purchase UL94 in larger quantities allows the County to offer UL94 for 
purchase at a price comparable to 100LL.  I believe that prior to the availability of UL94 at the 
County Airports, this price discrepancy was a significant barrier to UL94 adoption. 
27. 
Fuel sales have historically been a revenue source for the County’s Airport Enterprise 
Fund through the fuel flowage fees imposed on fuel sales at the County Airports.  I estimate that 
taking over the self-service island at RHV alone could generate over $100,000 in additional revenue 
annually for the Airport Enterprise Fund.  I anticipate that assuming operation of all the RHV Tanks 
would increase the potential revenue from fuel sales. 
