53. 
There has been no significant reduction in the number of aircraft based at County 
facilities at RHV due to the transition to the exclusive sale of unleaded avgas.  On January 1, 2022, 
there were 227 aircraft based at County facilities at RHV.  On September 30, 2022, there were 227 
aircraft based at County facilities at RHV.   
54. 
There has been no significant reduction in the number of aircraft based at County 
facilities at E16 due to the transition to the exclusive sale of unleaded avgas.  On January 1, 2022, 
there were 146 aircraft based at County facilities at E16.  On September 30, 2022, there were 151 
aircraft based at County facilities at E16. 
55. 
There have been no safety incidents at the County Airports relating to the 
unavailability of leaded avgas for purchase. 
Informal Dispute Resolution Efforts with Complainants 
56. 
Complainants have made no meaningful efforts to resolve the allegations stated in the 
Complaint with the County prior to filing the Complaint. 
57. 
The County has not received any written communication from any Complainant 
proposing an informal resolution to any allegation raised in the Complaint. 
58. 
The County has not received any written communication from any Complainant 
requesting a meeting to discuss the allegations raised in the Complaint. 
59. 
On December 13, 2021, Complainants filed an informal complaint with the FAA 
pursuant to 14 C.F.R. § 13.1 asserting that the unavailability of leaded avgas for purchase at the 
County Airports violates the County’s grant assurances to the FAA.  A true and correct copy of the 
December 13, 2021 letter is attached hereto as Exhibit K. 
60. On December 22, 2021, the County received a Notice of Informal Investigation Under 
14 CFR § 13.1 (“Part 13 Notice”) from Mark A. McClardy, Director, Airports Division for the 
Western-Pacific Region of the Federal Aviation Administration (“FAA”).  The Part 13 Notice 
included allegations relating to the availability of 100 octane leaded avgas for purchase at the 
County Airports.  Attachment 20 of the Complaint is a true and correct copy of the Part 13 Notice. 
