61. On January 11, 2022, the County sent Director McClardy a Response to Notice of 
Informal Investigation Under 14 C.F.R. § 13.1 via email.  Attachment 22 of the Complaint is a true 
and correct copy of the January 11, 2022 response County sent to Director McClardy. 
62. Since March 2022, County officials have met repeatedly with senior FAA officials and 
representatives from the Airports Division for the Western Pacific Region to discuss resolution of 
the issues raised in the Part 13 Notice. 
a. On March 9, 2022, senior FAA officials, including DOT Assistant Secretary 
Annie Petsonk, FAA Deputy Administrator Bradley Mims, and FAA Chief 
Counsel Marc Nichols, toured RHV and met with County Executive Jeffrey 
Smith, Supervisor Cindy Chavez, and other senior officials from County 
administration and the County Counsel’s office.  At that meeting, the FAA 
proposed drafting a memorandum of understanding (“MOU”) that would outline a 
mutually acceptable path forward toward resolving the issues detailed in the Part 
13 Notice.  The parties discussed that the MOU would include the County’s 
participation in a pilot demonstration initiative relating to the sale of fuel at the 
County Airports. 
b. On May 9, 2022, the County met with Deputy Administrator Mims to discuss 
resolution of issues raised in the Part 13 Notice. 
c. On July 18, 2022, the County met with FAA officials, including Deputy Director 
Mims, Assistant Administrator Shanetta Griffin, and Chief Counsel Nichols.  
Among other topics, the parties discussed changes to the availability of leaded 
avgas for purchase at the County Airports as a condition of participation in the 
pilot demonstration project.   
d. On September 16, 2022, the County met with FAA officials, including Deputy 
Administrator Mims and Director McClardy.  Among other topics, the parties 
discussed the FAA’s progress in developing the pilot demonstration initiative.  
Deputy Director Mims indicated that the pilot demonstration initiative was a 
priority for the FAA, and that FAA staff were meeting weekly on the MOU. 
