operations at the multitude of U.S. airports whose clients include approximately 
1000 +/- flight schools. 
Addressing past and ongoing lead particulate emissions and exposures caused by 
the general aviation piston-engine aircraft sector is long overdue. The FAA has 
been general aviation's handmaiden for going on four or more decades, working 
hand-in-hand with the sector to degrade the environment, degrade public health 

