(EAGLE) Regarding the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency Proposed Finding That Lead Emissions 
From Aircraft Engines That Operate on Leaded Fuel Cause or Contribute to Air Pollution That May 
Reasonably Be Anticipated To Endanger Public Health and Welfare – January 17, 2023 
Docket ID No. EPA–HQ–OAR–2022–0389 
 
 
  
   
 
Page3 
FAA authorization in 2021, commonly known as an AML-STC, or 
Approved Model List-Supplemental Type Certificate, to begin 
dispensing its G-100UL avgas. At the time of this writing, it is not yet 
available commercially. Additional unleaded fuel candidates are 
currently going through various test and evaluation protocols under the 
Piston Alternative Fuel Initiative (PAFI) program or the STC program 
before they may be authorized for production and distribution. These 
include Swift Fuels, Inc., which is pursuing STC authorization, while 
collaborative efforts between Afton Chemical and Phillips 66, as well as 
LyondellBasell and VP Racing are going through the PAFI testing 
program currently underway at the FAA’s Hughes Technical Center. 
EAGLE is committed to facilitate the successful transition to lead-
free aviation fuels for piston aircraft by the end of 2030, without 
compromising the safe and efficient operation of the General Aviation 
fleet. 
